      "title": "Actual full Boolean flip-energy Gaussian limit",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.E6",
        "edition": "SPHMC arXiv2609.06906v1; pinned SLT d0f506f0 and Mathlib db584cd6; Lean4.33.0",
        "anchor": "FIRST S4.E6 GaussianLSI background; SLT GaussianPoincare/Limit.lean L592-L1123 full shift-energy route, especially L1030-L1034 factor4; authored actual Boolean secant alternative",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Compact scalar prerequisite authored for omitted GaussianLSI background. External SLT real-product shift/permutation proof is source context, not a callable certificate. Authored Boolean route uses ASTIS36 and compiled Mathlib primitives; exact StatementSeal precedes proof. Integral of full finite sum is explicit; external sum of integrals is not silently substituted."
      },
      "statement": "For every real C2 compactly supported f, its derivative squared is integrable for the actual centered variance-one Gaussian. The literal normalized counting measure on all N Boolean coordinates integrates the sum of every squared f-value difference under a single-coordinate Boolean flip, including N=0. Its successor full-energy integral converges to four times the Gaussian derivative-square integral. No law, derivative bound, domain or limit certificate is a caller premise.",
      "assumptions": [
        "f:Real->Real, ContDiff Real2 f and HasCompactSupport f are the only analytic premises. Signed f, zero mass and zero f are included.",
        "The actual canonical finite Boolean carrier and literal cardinal-normalized counting law are fixed, not supplied certificates. Function.update flips exactly one coordinate; full energy is the sum over all coordinates with no one-half.",
        "C2compact internally supplies nonnegative bounds B,K for derivative and second derivative, hence global derivative Lipschitz control. Genuine finite-count L1 and Gaussian derivative-square L1 are conclusions.",
        "Only positive successor indices enter the limit. At N0 fullflip energy is an empty sum equal0; the separate derivative observer fprime(0)^2 may be nonzero.",
        "Authored compact scalar GaussianLSI background, not printed FIRST4.6 or a full GaussianLSI proof. Compact GaussianLSI, finite-Hilbert/noncompact extension, T2, main results and expected costs remain open."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Actual full Boolean flip-energy Gaussian limit",
          "tex": "\\mu_N=2^{-N}\\sum_{\\varepsilon\\in\\{0,1\\}^N}\\delta_\\varepsilon,\\quad S_N=N^{-1/2}\\sum_j\\sigma(\\varepsilon_j),\\quad D_N(\\varepsilon)=\\sum_{j=1}^{N}\\left[f(S_N(\\varepsilon^{(j)}))-f(S_N(\\varepsilon))\\right]^2;\\qquad \\int D_{N+1}\\,d\\mu_{N+1}\\longrightarrow4\\int (f\\prime)^2\\,d\\mathcal N(0,1)."
        }
      ],
